flowchart TD
  conv["Seeded conventions"]
  provider["Provider"]
  guard["bram-guard"]
  routes["Worklist routes"]
  tx["Provider transcripts"]
  claude["Claude<br/>· hook in project-local settings<br/>· loopback curl<br/>· JSONL under ~/.claude/projects<br/>· hook events"]
  codex["Codex<br/>· hook in ~/.codex/config.toml<br/>· intent and result files<br/>· rollouts under ~/.codex/sessions<br/>· rollout mtime"]
  opencode["OpenCode<br/>· plugin in .opencode/plugins<br/>· loopback curl<br/>· SQLite plus plugin events<br/>· --standalone, this terminal's token"]
  antigravity["Antigravity (agy)<br/>· hook group in .agents/hooks.json<br/>· loopback curl<br/>· exported from ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli<br/>· OSC 7501 turn state, menus read from the screen"]

  conv -.->|"loaded each session"| provider
  provider -->|"before every tool call"| guard
  provider -->|"resolve, mutate, commit, end"| routes
  provider -->|"the turns the host reads"| tx

  %% Each concrete provider is a Provider: a plain line, no arrowhead. Adding
  %% a provider is adding one box on this row.
  provider --- claude
  provider --- codex
  provider --- opencode
  provider --- antigravity

%% tip: Seeded conventions :: app/__shell/conventions.md, copied into managed projects by Setup. Each provider has its own way of loading it; following it is up to the model (dashed).
%% tip: Provider :: What every provider does, drawn once: loads the conventions, runs bram-guard before each tool call, reaches the Worklist routes, records turns the host reads. The four boxes below are the providers; each lists only where it differs.
%% tip: bram-guard :: One Rust binary with four registrations: claude-worklist, codex-worklist, opencode-worklist and antigravity-worklist all reach the same decider.
%% tip: Worklist routes :: The host's handlers for resolve, mutate, commit and end. Codex reaches them by a different transport but the same handlers.
%% tip: Provider transcripts :: Where each provider records turns. Bram reads them for turn state and the Transcript tab.
%% tip: loaded each session :: Dashed: the conventions reach the model as instructions; obeying them is up to the model.
%% tip: before every tool call :: The guard runs as a hook or plugin before each tool call and can deny it; a deny reaches the model as a tool error.
%% tip: resolve, mutate, commit, end :: The lifecycle routes every provider's agent calls, by curl or, for Codex, by files the host watches.
%% tip: the turns the host reads :: Each provider's own record of its turns, which Bram projects into one shape for the Transcript and search.
%% tip: Claude · hook in project-local settings · loopback curl · JSONL under ~/.claude/projects · hook events :: Claude Code, the claude command. Hook in the ignored .claude/settings.local.json; curl to the routes; one JSONL file per session; its hooks name the session and report turns.
%% tip: Codex · hook in ~/.codex/config.toml · intent and result files · rollouts under ~/.codex/sessions · rollout mtime :: Codex CLI, launched with --no-daemon. Its sandbox refuses loopback, so it writes .worklist-intent.json and reads .worklist-result.json; the host polls rollout mtime for turn end.
%% tip: OpenCode · plugin in .opencode/plugins · loopback curl · SQLite plus plugin events · --standalone, this terminal's token :: OpenCode, launched --standalone so its plugin carries this Bram's token; sessions are SQLite rows, and the plugin forwards turn boundaries.
%% tip: Antigravity (agy) · hook group in .agents/hooks.json · loopback curl · exported from ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli · OSC 7501 turn state, menus read from the screen :: Antigravity CLI, the agy command. Hooks in the project's .agents/hooks.json; turn state from OSC 7501 escape sequences; approval dialogs read from the screen; transcripts projected from agy's own store.
